      "writtenOn": "2024-11-13T02:26:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e mStagingBuffer is no longer always the DynamicUploader.\n\nThat\u0027s the problem. Now `DynamicUploader::ShouldFlush()` is always called in `Device::CopyStagingToBuffer()`[1] while actually `mStagingBuffer` for `mappedAtCreation` is not tracked with `DynamicUploader` any more, so that `ShouldFlush()` is totally unnecessary and I\u0027d like to fix it.\n\nI even find currently all the staging buffers that are intended to be released in\n`ReleaseStagingBuffer()` can be destroyed at once just like what we do for `mStagingbuffer`, so in the next CL we can also track such pieces of memory with `TrackStagingMemorySizeToRelease()`.\n\n[1] https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/Device.cpp;l\u003d2505",
      "parentUuid": "6ec79170_42cae0fa",
      "revId": "46619992f493ce2c2e649f575695c241e8eda8a5",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f23edbe5_79f33df9",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Buffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 894,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-12T13:08:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ShouldFlush is checked in CopyFromStagingToBuffer so if we do accounting we should do it before that call. But also IMHO we should not do it in DynamicUploader.",
      "revId": "46619992f493ce2c2e649f575695c241e8eda8a5",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5e5ec12e_ab708cca",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Buffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 894,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000019
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-13T02:26:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK but I think we should track the total memory of `mStagingBuffer` for `mappedAtCreation` because if we can release `mStagingBuffer` soon we can better recycle the memory (e.g. the underlying D3D12 heap) for future `mappedAtCreation`.\n\nI\u0027d like to solve the problem that:\n- An application (e.g. LLM) initializes all the input buffers (e.g. the input weights which can be several GB) with `mappedAtCreation \u003d\u003d true`.\n- Currently calling `unmap` won\u0027t manually trigger the execution of the pending\n  command list, which means the memory in UPLOAD heap cannot be released.\n- The current solution is on the JS side calling several empty `queue.submit([])`.\n- Do you think if we should commit the pending command list if we have allocated\n  too much staging memory to avoid such empty submit?",
      "parentUuid": "f23edbe5_79f33df9",
      "revId": "46619992f493ce2c2e649f575695c241e8eda8a5",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "52fabd52_012ce565",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Buffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 894,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-13T14:30:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes we should commit the pending command list (at some point, maybe we should wait a bit to aggregate more than 64kb, as that limit is small and could cause a LOT of submits, but that\u0027s another topic) for mappedAtCreation + Unmap as well. However DynamicUploader is no longer the correct place for that if the memory that we want to cause flushes with is no longer allocated with the DynamicUploader. What do you think of moving that logic maybe to ExecutionQueue with a number of bytes waiting for upload and would be freed eventually after a submit?\n\nLoko would putting that logic on ExecutionQueue sound good to you?",
      "parentUuid": "5e5ec12e_ab708cca",
      "revId": "46619992f493ce2c2e649f575695c241e8eda8a5",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
